  "status_text": "Three dots, two lines, exactly six steps. Lean checked a circuit that decides whether the selected dots touch both lines of a three-point path. Whenever they do, it also says whether exactly one end of each line is selected. Every circuit doing all three jobs needs at least six gates in total, including at least four AND or OR gates and at least two NOT gates. One circuit meets all three limits. Each gate reads at most two earlier wires, with constants free. Next comes the same total-gate question for the triangle (L-lib-1200).",
